      "A **pressure injury** (pressure ulcer, bed sore) is localised damage to skin and underlying soft tissue over a **bony prominence or under a medical device**, caused by sustained **pressure or pressure plus shear** that exceeds capillary closing pressure (about 32 mmHg) for long enough to cause ischaemia - staged by **NPIAP** from stage 1 to 4 plus unstageable and deep tissue injury, it is largely preventable by **risk scoring (Braden), 2-hourly repositioning, the right support surface, moisture control and nutrition**, and is treated by off-loading first and dressings second.",
